comments.body:
@StefanieSenger Thanks for the context! That makes total sense regarding the broader namespace refactoring effort by @lucyleeow.

I went ahead and opened a quick, targeted PR #34493  to implement check_same_namespace for PCA to align it with the linear models in the short term. All the CI checks and linters are passing. @david-cortes-intel 

If the broader design ends up superseding this patch globally later on, I completely understand if the PR gets closed in favor of that larger solution. Thanks for the guidance.

Following up on the OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS#5414 link: that issue has since been root-caused by the OpenBLAS maintainer. The SME SGEMM direct kernel (`sgemm_direct_sme1_2VLx2VL.S`) inadvertently uses register `x18`, which is reserved on macOS. A fix is in progress (a separate `VORTEXM4` target is being split out).

That lines up with everything seen here: float32-only (SGEMM), M4-only (the `vortexm4`/SME path), and nightly-only (the nightly scipy-openblas wheel ships the SME kernel, while released wheels take the older `VORTEX` path). So this looks like purely the OpenBLAS M4 SME kernel rather than anything in scikit-learn, numpy, or scipy proper.

@betatim to your point about routing this to numpy/scipy: it seems to narrow down to OpenBLAS itself. @rcap107 it might not be worth opening a separate upstream issue, since OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS#5414 already covers it with a fix underway. Probably just a matter of waiting for the fixed OpenBLAS to land in the nightly wheels.
